  "live_records": {
    "q-193579": {
      "dom_id": "step-q193579",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Daniel reads $2\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ chapters of a book every hour. How many chapters does he read in $3$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out the number of chapters Daniel reads, we need to multiply $2\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ by $3.$\n\nFirst, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(2\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe also write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}.\n$$\n\nSo now, we need to solve the following multiplication problem:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}\\times \\frac{3}{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the first fraction's denominator ($3$) and the second fraction's numerator ($3$) have a common factor of $3.$ \n\nTherefore, we can simplify our problem by swapping the denominators first and then multiplying the resulting fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3}\\times \\frac{3}{1} & =\\frac{7}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{1}\\times 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Daniel reads $7$ chapters in three hours.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
