    "q-193555": {
      "dom_id": "step-q193555",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Mario fills three bottles with water. If the capacity of every bottle is $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ liters, how much water did he use to fill the bottles?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the total volume of water used to fill the bottles, we need to multiply $3$ by $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nFirst, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(1\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe also write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}.\n$$\n\nSo now, we need to solve the following multiplication problem:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the first fraction's numerator ($3$) and the second fraction's denominator ($3$) have a common factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify our problem by swapping the denominators first and then multiplying the resulting fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3} & =\\frac{3}{3}\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =1\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mario used $4$ liters of water to fill the bottles.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-193555-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$7$ liters",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"23\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> liters "
            },
            {
